<title>USA: Strouds Q4, year loss with charge vs profit.</title>
<headline>Strouds Q4, year loss with charge vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>CITY OF INDUSTRY, Calif. 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter Ended  Fiscal Year Ended</p>
<p>				   Mar 1,   Mar 2,    Mar 1,   Mar 2,</p>
<p>				    1997	1996     1997	1996</p>
<p>		   (13 weeks)  (14 weeks)   (52 weeks) (53 weeks)</p>
<p> Net Sales		    $58,842  $55,788  $209,778 $190,316</p>
<p>Cost of sales, including</p>
<p>   buying and occupancy    43,393   38,290   150,625  131,179</p>
<p>Selling and administrative</p>
<p>   expense		     17,467   14,898    63,963   54,175</p>
<p>Restructure and asset  </p>
<p>   impairment charges	18,050	---    18,050	---</p>
<p> Amortization			64	 64	 258	258</p>
<p>Operating income (loss)</p>
<p>				 (20,132)    2,536  (23,118)    4,704</p>
<p> Other income		     143	198	 508	349</p>
<p> Interest expense, net	(706)    (265)   (1,846)    (735)</p>
<p>Income (loss) before</p>
<p>   income taxes	    (20,695)    2,469  (24,456)    4,318</p>
<p>Income tax (expense) benefit</p>
<p>				    1,320  (1,004)     2,488  (1,748)</p>
<p> Net income (loss)	 (19,375)    1,465  (21,968)    2,570</p>
<p>Net income (loss) per share</p>
<p>				   (2.28)     0.17    (2.58)     0.30</p>
<p>Weighted average shares</p>
<p>   outstanding		  8,531    8,718     8,521    8,622</p>
<p>NOTES: Full company name is Strounds Inc.</p>
<p>The company said Q4 results include a charge of $18.05 million as part of a restructuring plan. The plan includes closing or disposing of 16 stores over two years, asset impairment charges and other cost reduction measures.</p>
<p>The company said Q4 comparable store sales dropped 3.1 percent. Year-end comparable store sales rose 0.1 percent.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
